#: ckanext/theme_ejemplo/templates/home/snippets/about_text.html:1
msgid ""
"<h1>The IHP Water Information Network System (IHP-WINS)</h1> <p>The "
"<strong>Intergovernmental Hydrological Programme's Water Information Network "
"System (IHP-WINS)</strong> is designed to promote the <em>sharing and "
"dissemination of water-related data and information</em> among countries, "
"organizations, and stakeholders involved in water resources management, as "
"part of the UNESCO IHP mandate.</p> <p>The main objective of IHP-WINS is "
"<strong>to enhance the availability, accessibility, and usability of water-"
"related information, with a focus on supporting evidence-based decision-"
"making and sustainable water resources management</strong>. It aims to "
"facilitate the exchange of data, knowledge, and best practices among "
"stakeholders at various levels, including national, regional, and global "
"scales.</p> <p>IHP-WINS provides a platform for integrating and harmonizing "
"water-related data and information from diverse sources, such as monitoring "
"networks, research institutions, government agencies, and international "
"organizations. It promotes the use of standardized data formats and metadata "
"to ensure compatibility and interoperability of information across different "
"systems and platforms.</p> <h2>Key features of IHP-WINS include:</h2> <ul> "
"<li><strong>Data Sharing:</strong> IHP-WINS facilitates the sharing of water-"
"related data, including hydrological data, water quality data, and climate "
"data. It provides a secure and centralized repository for storing and "
"accessing these datasets, allowing users to contribute their data and access "
"data shared by others.</li> <li><strong>Information Exchange:</strong> The "
"platform promotes collaboration and knowledge exchange among water "
"professionals, researchers, policymakers, and other stakeholders. It enables "
"the sharing of research findings, reports, publications, and other relevant "
"information related to water resources management.</li> <li><strong>Decision "
"Support:</strong> IHP-WINS supports decision-making processes by providing "
"tools and services for data visualization, analysis, and modeling. It helps "
"stakeholders assess water availability, water quality, and water-related "
"risks, contributing to informed decision-making for sustainable water "
"management.</li> <li><strong>Capacity Building:</strong> The platform serves "
"as a resource hub for capacity-building materials, training modules, and "
"educational resources related to water resources management. It facilitates "
"the dissemination of knowledge and best practices, fostering the development "
"of technical skills and expertise in water-related disciplines.</li> "
"<li><strong>Collaboration and Networking:</strong> IHP-WINS promotes "
"collaboration and networking among water professionals and organizations "
"through its community-based approach. It facilitates the establishment of "
"partnerships, the exchange of experiences, and the creation of communities of"
" practice focused on specific water management topics.</li> </ul> <p>Through "
"IHP-WINS, UNESCO's Intergovernmental Hydrological Programme aims to "
"strengthen international cooperation, improve data availability, and enhance "
"the understanding and management of water resources worldwide. The initiative"
" contributes to the achievement of sustainable development goals related to "
"water and supports countries in their efforts to address water-related "
"challenges and promote integrated water resources management.</p> <p>Overall,"
" IHP-WINS plays a vital role in advancing water governance, supporting "
"evidence-based decision-making, and fostering international cooperation for "
"sustainable water resources management.</p>"
msgstr ""

